---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms for official Lootr app releases and services."
  effectiveDate="28 July 2026"
>
  <aside class="legal-summary legal-summary-warning">
    <strong>Alpha software</strong>
    <p>
      Lootr can contain defects or incorrect calculations. Keep an independent
      backup and verify important figures.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lootr does not give financial, tax, accounting, or legal advice.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Agreement and operator</h2>
    <p>
      Joashdev operates the official Lootr project from the Philippines. These
      Terms cover official releases, the website, and the feedback service.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you install or use an official release, you accept these Terms. If
      you do not accept them, do not use official Lootr services.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms do not reduce your rights under the open-source license.
      Independent forks can use different terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 18 years old. You must also have the legal capacity
      to accept these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Product boundary</h2>
    <p>
      Lootr is a manual, offline-first recordkeeping tool. Lootr is not a bank,
      lender, broker, adviser, accountant, tax preparer, or fiduciary.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lootr is not a credit-reporting agency, payment processor, or money
      transmitter. Lootr does not hold, transfer, or invest money.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lootr does not connect to a bank or verify the data that you enter.
    </p>
    <p>
      Forecasts, reports, categories, OCR, voice text, and AI suggestions are
      estimates. Check each result before you make a financial decision.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Alpha risks and backups</h2>
    <p>
      Lootr is prerelease software. Its features, file formats, compatibility,
      and availability can change.
    </p>
    <p>
      A defect, failed migration, device failure, uninstall, or operating-system
      action can cause data loss.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep a tested independent backup. Protect your exports, receipts, device,
      passcodes, and recovery data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Do not use official Lootr services for these actions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Break the law or violate another person's rights.</li>
      <li>Publish private data without authority.</li>
      <li>Attack, overload, probe, or bypass a security control.</li>
      <li>Misrepresent a modified build as an official release.</li>
      <li>Upload malware, passwords, or financial databases.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These rules do not prohibit lawful security research or open-source
      modification. Use synthetic data and report vulnerabilities privately.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Your content and public feedback</h2>
    <p>
      You own the content that you create. You control your local ledger
      content.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you submit feedback, you direct Lootr to publish the approved report.
      You must separately approve each screenshot.
    </p>
    <p>
      You give Lootr a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free license for the
      submitted content.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lootr can host, copy, display, and use this content to operate, secure,
      document, and improve the project.
    </p>
    <p>
      Submit only content that you have the right to share. Public systems can
      copy and index your report.
    </p>
    <p>
      Complete removal from every notification, cache, fork, or archive can be
      impossible.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Open-source license and marks</h2>
    <p>
      Lootr uses the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later. The
      repository contains the complete license.
    </p>
    <p>
      That license controls your rights to copy, inspect, change, and distribute
      covered code. These Terms do not add a code restriction.
    </p>
    <p>
      The code license does not give permission to present a modified build as
      an official Lootr release.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Third-party terms</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub, Cloudflare, operating-system speech services, and app stores have
      their own terms. You must follow applicable third-party terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you get Lootr from Apple, Apple's <a
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
        >Standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a
      > also applies.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms do not replace Apple's standard agreement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how official Lootr
      services process data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not use public feedback for a security report or privacy request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. Fees and store terms</h2>
    <p>
      The current alpha has no Lootr subscription or in-app purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before Lootr adds a paid feature, it will show the price and all payment
      terms. These include renewal, cancellation, tax, and refund terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Store rules and mandatory consumer rights also apply.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>11. Ending use</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using Lootr at any time. You can delete individual records
      or remove all app data through your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lootr can restrict an online service to stop abuse, meet a legal duty, or
      protect the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      A loss of an online V1 service does not delete the ledger on your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>12. Warranty disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent that law permits, Lootr provides official software and
      services “as is” and “as available.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Lootr does not promise uninterrupted, secure, accurate, complete, or
      compatible operation.
    </p>
    <p>
      The AGPL contains more warranty terms for covered software. Mandatory
      consumer rights remain in effect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>13. Liability limit</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent that law permits, Lootr is not liable for indirect,
      incidental, special, consequential, or punitive loss.
    </p>
    <p>
      This limit includes loss of data, profit, revenue, opportunity, or
      expected savings.
    </p>
    <p>
      This section does not limit liability when the law prohibits that limit.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      Philippine law governs these Terms. Mandatory consumer rights and forums
      in your home jurisdiction remain in effect.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before you file a claim, send Joashdev a private message. Give Joashdev a
      reasonable time to resolve the issue.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>15. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Lootr can change these Terms when the project changes. Lootr will identify
      a material change in the app, website, or release notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      New terms apply from their stated effective date. If you continue to use
      Lootr, you accept the new terms where law permits.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a private legal or privacy question, use the <a
        href="https://github.com/joashdev/lootr/security/advisories/new"
        >private contact form</a
      >. Identify the request in the title.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not attach financial records, backups, receipts, identity documents,
      or passwords.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
